# Milestone: M3
# Covers: watchers registered in order A-then-B fire in registration order
#         when both conditions become true simultaneously (row 12 §6 watcher
#         eval determinism — active_watchers_head preserves insertion order).
#
# blocked: chk-runner urbi_step driver path not implemented (T39)
# matrix-row: scheduler-fifo
#
# Reason: verifying watcher firing order requires installing watchers via
# `at (cond) body` syntax, which produces watcher body strands that run via
# OP_FORK_DETACH (spawn_body_coroutine path).  The chk runner uses the REPL
# (urbi_vm_run path) — fork opcodes return TypeError there.  Additionally, the
# `at` keyword emit path requires the M5 reactive runtime wiring (condition
# closures, install/uninstall, edge/level detection).  The watcher pool and
# dirty-set infrastructure is wired at M3 but the full activation requires M5.
#
# When M5 reactive runtime + urbi_step chk driver land, implement this by:
#   var log = ""
#   at (true) { log = log + "A" | stop }
#   at (true) { log = log + "B" | stop }
#   -- step to quiescent --
#   log
#   --- expected output (registration FIFO ordering) ---
#   [00000001] "AB"
